Subject: Fuse Object Literal Field Stores Into One Opcode

What this does
  An eligible object literal compiles to OP_object followed by one
  OP_define_field per property. In resolve_labels those N defines are deleted and
  replaced by a single OP_object_fill [u16 n][u16 tpl_idx], which stores the N
  values sitting on the operand stack into the template's slots 0..n-1 and leaves
  the object where it was.

Why we need it
  Each OP_define_field costs a dispatch, a four-byte inline atom decode, a tag
  test, an exotic test, a find_own_property hash lookup and a flags test before it
  reaches the store. The transformation is done at compile time, so it is baked
  into the shipped bytecode and the saved ops are never executed at all.

What it adds
  One opcode, taken over the slot of OP_nip1, which nothing emits. Its encoding is
  OP_FMT_npop_u16, the same shape OP_eval already uses, so compute_stack_size()
  and the bytecode reader and writer model the variable pop with no new case. A
  site is copied only when every property is a static plain data key, no key
  repeats, and the recorded define count matches the template's slot count; the
  rewriter is all-or-nothing, and js_create_function re-derives every template
  index from the same liveness predicate before it allocates anything.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No. 9999 owns the version number and carries this patch's rebuilt builtins.

